														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4378701">
									

<p>The heartrate is reducing BY 1bpm every 30 seconds (aka reducing by 2 beats every minute) until it reaches a final rate of 1bpm. So if your original heartrate was 60, it would take only about half an hour to end up at 1bpm but it would be going down at the same rate the entire time, not drop suddenly the entire amount. If you're a person with an unusually fast BPM of 120, it would take about an hour to get down to 1.</p>
<p>How that interacts with the natural fear response (of an increased heartrate) once it's been noted by sensors that their heartrate is plummeting, we'll never know 😆</p>

